  <title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00717</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology</md:title>
    <md:uuid>202bd07d-2ab2-41fa-8101-082d2ceaaf1c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Linear models can also be found by hand in some situations when the data follows a linear pattern since the slope remains the same between data points. </para>
<para><emphasis>Linear Models from Tables</emphasis></para>
<blockquote>
  <newline/><para>For 1 - 4, use the scenario and table below:</para>
  <para>The table below shows the number of songs Marcus will have in his collection as he adds new songs each month.</para>

<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Number of months, \(t\)</emphasis></entry><entry>0</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Number of songs, \(N\)</emphasis></entry><entry>200</entry>
      <entry>215</entry>
      <entry>230</entry>
      <entry>245</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
</blockquote>

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="50701f9a-8db4-46eb-a7b0-673edcb2a852"><problem><para>
      <para> What is the initial amount of songs, or the \(y\)-intercept of this situation? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>200</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 200.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(N = 15t + 200\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="487937b8-cda6-4e24-836b-d9802cb72dac"><problem><para>
      <para> How many songs will Marcus have in 8 months? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>320</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 320.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#7-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write the equation of the linear model that represents the situation in slope-intercept form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(H= \frac12 x\) +12.5\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
